{"id": "169733", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=169733", "title": "Hoshiarpur", "text": "Hoshiarpur is a city in the Doaba region of the Punjab of India. It stands at 300 m (982 m) altitude so it's a little cooler than the nearby sultry river plains, with forested upland terrain.\nGet in.\nThe regional airport is Amritsar ('), more snappily known as Sri Guru Ram Dass Jee International Airport. A cab from there will take 2 hours 30 min to Hoshiarpur. Otherwise fly into Delhi ('), which has extensive transcontinental connections, and travel overland.\nConnect.\nChandigarh, Nawasher, Himachal,"}
